,"review_status":"verified","doi":"10.64972/dea.2026.v5i2.1755d:58-72","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.64972/dea.2026.v5i2.1755d:58-72","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.64972/dea.2026.v5i2.1755d:58-72","url":"https://doi.org/10.64972/dea.2026.v5i2.1755d:58-72","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:31:05Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-c3836a6d1973a6ee","title":"Noise-Informed Diffusion-Generated Image Detection With Anomaly Attention","title_zh":"","year":2025,"publication_date":"2025-01-01","abstract":"With the rapid development of image generation technologies, especially the advancement of Diffusion Models, the quality of synthesized images has significantly improved, raising concerns among researchers about information security. To mitigate the malicious abuse of diffusion models, diffusion-generated image detection has proven to be an effective countermeasure. However, a key challenge for forgery detection is generalising to diffusion models not seen during training. In this paper, we address this problem by focusing on image noise. We observe that images from different diffusion models share similar noise patterns, distinct from genuine images. Building upon this insight, we introduce a novel Noise-Aware Self-Attention (NASA) module that focuses on noise regions to capture anomalous patterns. To implement a SOTA detection model, we incorporate NASA into Swin Transformer, forming an novel detection architecture NASA-Swin. Additionally, we employ a cross-modality fusion embedding to combine RGB and noise images, along with a channel mask strategy to enhance feature learning from both modalities. Extensive experiments demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach in enhancing detection capabilities for diffusion-generated images. When encountering unseen generation methods, our approach achieves the state-of-the-art performance.","authors":[{"id":"a5055116095","name":"Weinan Guan","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-4269545a834014","name":"Wei Wang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5042160852","name":"Bo Peng","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5053180123","name":"Ziwen He","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5017743261","name":"Jing Dong","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-1a49f155f27149","name":"Haonan Cheng","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":["i19820366","i200845125","i4210100255","i4210112150","i4210165038","i75689368","institution:0af8b0b3be8e7963","institution:157163d25dac880f","institution:3afb6cc453e0a8d9","institution:69309405e04976ec","institution:707f47de3ba40880","institution:985443a2d7239406"],"venue":{"id":"venue-f69a9dd74f3931","name":"IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security","short_name":"TIFS","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"1","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13028.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Engineering","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13028.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["synthetic_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/tifs.2025.3573161","arxiv_id":"2506.16743","openalex_id":"W4410853187","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tifs.2025.3573161","citation_count":5,"provenance":[{"source":"authorized_seed","source_id":"","url":"https://openalex.org/W4410853187","query":"","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T00:00:00Z"},{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4410853187","url":"https://openalex.org/W4410853187","query":"diffusion generated image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/tifs.2025.3573161","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tifs.2025.3573161","query":"diffusion generated image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:29:34Z"},{"source":"arxiv","source_id":"2506.16743","url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2506.16743v1","query":"diffusion generated image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:34:35Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-d895faaa0ed398ee","title":"Stacking Brick by Brick: Aligned Feature Isolation for Incremental Face Forgery Detection","title_zh":"","year":2025,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"2148467637","name":"Jikang Cheng","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2316152520","name":"Zhiyuan Yan","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5100386145","name":"Ying Zhang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-55774fbeb49c94","name":"Li Hao","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5039758355","name":"Jiaxin Ai","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5070093927","name":"Qin Zou","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2316009795","name":"Chen Li","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5100741750","name":"Zhongyuan Wang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-cvpr","name":"2025 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR)","short_name":"CVPR","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CCF","level":"A","category":"人工智能","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"第七版（2026）","source_url":"https://www.ccf.org.cn/Academic_Evaluation/By_category/","verified_at":"2026-07-16"}]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/cvpr52734.2025.01300","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr52734.2025.01300","citation_count":10,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/cvpr52734.2025.01300","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr52734.2025.01300","query":"image forgery localization @ CVPR","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:41:50Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e4ba3b09938803ee","title":"A Large-scale Universal Evaluation Benchmark For Face Forgery Detection","title_zh":"","year":2024,"publication_date":"2024-06-13","abstract":"With the rapid development of AI-generated content (AIGC) technology, the production of realistic fake facial images and videos that deceive human visual perception has become possible. Consequently, various face forgery detection techniques have been proposed to identify such fake facial content. However, evaluating the effectiveness and generalizability of these detection techniques remains a significant challenge. To address this, we have constructed a large-scale evaluation benchmark called DeepFaceGen, aimed at quantitatively assessing the effectiveness of face forgery detection and facilitating the iterative development of forgery detection technology. DeepFaceGen consists of 776,990 real face image/video samples and 773,812 face forgery image/video samples, generated using 34 mainstream face generation techniques. During the construction process, we carefully consider important factors such as content diversity, fairness across ethnicities, and availability of comprehensive labels, in order to ensure the versatility and convenience of DeepFaceGen. Subsequently, DeepFaceGen is employed in this study to evaluate and analyze the performance of 13 mainstream face forgery detection techniques from various perspectives. Through extensive experimental analysis, we derive significant findings and propose potential directions for future research. The code and dataset for DeepFaceGen are available at https://github.com/HengruiLou/DeepFaceGen.","authors":[{"id":"a5058864361","name":"Yijun Bei","orcid":"0000-0001-5720-6374","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5004651483","name":"Hengrui Lou","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5034157866","name":"Jinsong Geng","orcid":"0000-0003-3389-9051","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5010410284","name":"Erteng Liu","orcid":"0009-0005-6502-4454","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5060524512","name":"Lechao Cheng","orcid":"0000-0002-7546-9052","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5100612510","name":"Jie Song","orcid":"0000-0001-7610-0209","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5026532752","name":"Mingli Song","orcid":"0000-0003-2621-6048","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5043914348","name":"Zunlei Feng","orcid":"0000-0001-8640-8434","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-14849488429a12","name":"arXiv (Cornell University)","short_name":"","type":"preprint","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"benchmark","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2406.09181","arxiv_id":"2406.09181","openalex_id":"W4399695708","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09181","citation_count":6,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4399695708","url":"https://openalex.org/W4399695708","query":"scene text image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"d00215813d61621c9fb3188a119db69febfa58c6","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d00215813d61621c9fb3188a119db69febfa58c6","query":"universal fake image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:40:00Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1145/3746027.3758194","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3746027.3758194","query":"image forgery localization @ ACM Multimedia","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:42:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-47bd656e99c84dee","title":"Advancements in Image Steganalysis: Integrating Deep Learning and Statistical Feature Analysis","title_zh":"","year":2024,"publication_date":"","abstract":"With the intriguing concept of Steganography and Steganalysis, this research paper focuses on analyzing images to detect cover images. The system core is the Deep convolutional neural networks (CNNs), capable of automatically recognizing patterns indicative of steganography. Deep convolutional neural networks combined with Markov features-based analysis, spatial pixel distribution and subtractive pixel adjacency matrices to analyze the statistical properties can significantly improve anomaly detection and steganalysis. The Gabor Filter Residual algorithm detects hidden messages by recognizing anomalies in the residuals left after the Gabor Filters application. Ensemble classifiers contribute to creating a robustsystem with better generalizability. A multimodal deep learning framework assimilates various sourced data, adding the ability to detect a broad range of steganography methods. The traditional RS Analysis method can compare/create a baseline for the system's effectiveness. Lastly, Lightweight Steganalysis with block-wise pruning reduces the computational cost and is beneficial in resourceconstrained environments.","authors":[{"id":"author-208c3bf8540b7d","name":"Amoghavarsha K","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-9dc1626e3ead8c","name":"Anagha Upadyaya","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-e29b28bc54a31a","name":"Amogha Upadyaya","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-068cecea4e87c0","name":"Priya P Prabhu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-95c3e68f5174a8","name":"J Somasekar","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-d0c484503f8f9b","name":"2024 Recent Advances in Sustainable Engineering and Future Technologies (RASEFT)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/raseft61414.2024.00017","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/raseft61414.2024.00017","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/raseft61414.2024.00017","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/raseft61414.2024.00017","query":"deep learning image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:01Z"},{"sourc