ng Approximate Entropy","title_zh":"","year":2012,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-4719d73a940fcd","name":"Hafiz Malik","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-d86697890d3a1b","name":"K. P. Subbalakshmi","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-c70e08001b2830","name":"R. Chandramouli","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-f69a9dd74f3931","name":"IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security","short_name":"TIFS","type":"journal","issn":"1556-6013","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"1","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13028.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Engineering","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13028.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/tifs.2011.2169058","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tifs.2011.2169058","citation_count":13,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/tifs.2011.2169058","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tifs.2011.2169058","query":"image steganalysis @ IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:12Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-64e3d1b8bb4129ee","title":"Optimizing pixel predictors for steganalysis","title_zh":"","year":2012,"publication_date":"2012-02-08","abstract":"A standard way to design steganalysis features for digital images is to choose a pixel predictor, use it to compute a noise residual, and then form joint statistics of neighboring residual samples (co-occurrence matrices). This paper proposes a general data-driven approach to optimizing predictors for steganalysis. First, a local pixel predictor is parametrized and then its parameters are determined by solving an optimization problem for a given sample of cover and stego images and a given cover source. Our research shows that predictors optimized to detect a specific case of steganography may be vastly different than predictors optimized for the cover source only. The results indicate that optimized predictors may improve steganalysis by a rather non-negligible margin. Furthermore, we construct the predictors sequentially - having optimized k predictors, design the k + 1st one with respect to the combined feature set built from all k predictors. In other words, given a feature space (image model) extend (diversify) the model in a selected direction (functional form of the predictor) in a way that maximally boosts detection accuracy.","authors":[{"id":"a5060462615","name":"Vojtěch Holub","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i123946342"]},{"id":"a5081020569","name":"Jessica Fridrich","orcid":"0009-0003-6516-628X","institution_ids":["i123946342"]}],"institution_ids":["i123946342"],"venue":{"id":"venue-28757b3c57cb1d","name":"Proceedings of SPIE, the International Society for Optical Engineering/Proceedings of SPIE","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1117/12.905753","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2041651059","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.905753","citation_count":22,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2041651059","url":"https://openalex.org/W2041651059","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1117/12.905753","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.905753","query":"image steganalysis @ USENIX Security","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:27Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-40b5fc5f5da92aee","title":"RTCSP ’ 10 1 FEATURE BASED CLASSIFICATION SYSTEM FOR JPEG STEGANALYSIS","title_zh":"","year":2010,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"152279542","name":"D. Shankar","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"a2be67423912229921096ef00b2f0f061b4d5967","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/a2be67423912229921096ef00b2f0f061b4d5967","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"a2be67423912229921096ef00b2f0f061b4d5967","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/a2be67423912229921096ef00b2f0f061b4d5967","query":"cover stego image classification","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:11:02Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-5b118c1b8afad4ee","title":"Steganalysis based on Markov Model of Thresholded Prediction-Error Image","title_zh":"","year":2006,"publication_date":"2006-07-01","abstract":"A steganalysis system based on 2-D Markov chain of thresholded prediction-error image is proposed in this paper. Image pixels are predicted with their neighboring pixels, and the prediction-error image is generated by subtracting the prediction value from the pixel value and then thresholded with a predefined threshold. The empirical transition matrixes of Markov chain along the horizontal, vertical and diagonal directions serve as features for steganalysis. Support vector machines (SVM) are utilized as classifier. The effectiveness of the proposed system has been demonstrated by extensive experimental investigation. The detection rate for Cox et al.'s non-blind spread spectrum (SS) data hiding method, Piva et al.'s blind SS method, and a generic QIM method (as embedding data rate being 0.1 bpp (bits per pixel)) are all above 90% over an image database consisting of approximately 4000 images. For generic LSB method (with various embedding data rates), our steganalysis system achieves a detection rate above 85% as the embedding data rate is 0.1 bpp and above","authors":[{"id":"a5110235608","name":"Dekun Zou","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i118118575"]},{"id":"a5011290120","name":"Yun Shi","orcid":"0000-0001-7370-0663","institution_ids":["i118118575"]},{"id":"a5100755437","name":"Wei Su","orcid":"0000-0003-0952-0398","institution_ids":["i118118575"]},{"id":"a5111714804","name":"Guorong Xuan","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i116953780"]}],"institution_ids":["i116953780","i118118575"],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icme.2006.262792","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2136492908","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icme.2006.262792","citation_count":89,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2136492908","url":"https://openalex.org/W2136492908","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/icme.2006.262792","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icme.2006.262792","query":"rich model image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:06Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-cafb72d264203eee","title":"Model based algorithm for singular point detection from fingerprint images","title_zh":"","year":null,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-50dd1be9229ea3","name":"Nannan Wu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2257357644","name":"Jie Zhou","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-d64701913d0b4f","name":"2004 International Conference on Image Processing, 2004. ICIP '04.","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/icip.2004.1419441","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/icip.2004.1419441","citation_count":6,"provenance":[{"source":"cros